WEBVTT

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:09.790
<i>The countless flowers,
enveloped in light…</i>

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:20.160
<i>…gaze at tomorrow
with unwavering eyes.</i>

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:39.350
<i>Everyone wishes for me to be pure…</i>

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:46.800
<i>…but what can I bring
with me to the frayed skies?</i>

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:53.900
<i>What I’ve made my own
by breaking off flowers in bloom…</i>

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:59.550
<i>All such sinful things…</i>

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:07.020
<i>Why did I stop making
promises with the future?</i>

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:14.330
<i>Because even if I try
to run far from all the pain…</i>

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:21.030
<i>…a cold wind rustles
my hair… Don’t you see?</i>

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:28.260
<i>Where can I ever find the answer?</i>

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:36.100
I wanted you to move on to
the next phase of your life.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:43.240
I can’t lose face in the high council.
Chor Tempest can’t go on as it has.

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:57.300
Until the repairs on the Arcus Prima
are completed, Chor Tempest…

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:03.260
…will board the Messis and be
charged with border reconnaissance.

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:06.300
What? We’re boarding that thing?

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:07.770
I’m a bit…

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:11.740
Don’t be unreasonable. You should
just be thankful Chor Tempest…

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:15.280
She’s right.
That old boat should do just fine.

00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:18.780
I don’t mind at all!

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:34.300
<b>Birds in a Cage</b>

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:04.620
Hey, are we really
gonna live here, all together?

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:09.760
Floe, you’d better save your
complaining till you’ve secured a spot.

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:12.370
The beds on the window side
are first come, first served.

00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:14.080
No way!

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:22.760
Best regards, Floe.

00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:24.760
Best regards, Aer.

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:35.980
Big Sister, do you think we’ll
be living here for a long time?

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:38.780
Just like we can’t
change what’s happened…

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:41.280
…there’s no telling
what’s in the future.

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:44.030
Right…

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:46.780
You may be right about that, Kaim.

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:58.140
Yun, where’s Mamina?

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:00.550
I have no idea.

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:02.010
I see…

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:09.320
We believe the damage
was caused in transit.

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:13.120
The communication-wire
ejectors have come a bit loose.

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:15.460
Can you manage
without replacing parts?

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:17.590
Yes, somehow…

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:21.970
There’ll be a severe shortage of
replacement parts. Keep that in mind.

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:23.240
Right.

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:26.400
Looks like you’re having
a hard time, Waporif.

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:30.040
Not compared to
you sibyllae. You’re all so noble.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:33.250
Everything must seem new to you…
I’m sure you’re taken aback.

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:39.210
Noble you say? We can’t afford
to worry about being noble right now.

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:40.690
Anyway, I…

00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:43.510
As long as you can
fly a Simoun, correct?

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:45.300
Absolutely.

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:57.960
Then that’s how I’d like
the reconnaissance tasks divided.

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:02.040
Very well.
But if I may, Sibylla Dominüra…

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:03.770
What is it?

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:09.030
Chor Tempest is the finest chor and
the pride of Simulacrum Kyuukoku.

00:05:09.670 --> 00:05:14.160
Though my crew and I are
greatly honored by your presence…

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:17.850
…why were you assigned
to an old front-line vessel…

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:21.800
Captain, the inconvenience
is written all over your face.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:23.800
N-No, not at all.

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:26.760
No matter. You’re quite right.

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:32.310
And someone from a different chain
of command is invading your bridge.

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:35.410
Very well, Sibylla Dominüra.

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:38.600
I will refrain from
asking you anything more.

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:47.820
Sibylla, please stop… Sibylla!

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:50.090
It’s beneath you…

00:05:50.090 --> 00:05:55.350
Don’t worry, I’ve worked in
kitchens since I was a child.

00:05:55.850 --> 00:05:59.450
I really enjoy doing this, you know.

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:47.260
This area along the Shoukoku border
is most vulnerable to invasion.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:50.760
This may be a scheduled recon
flight, but don’t drop your guard.

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:53.510
Scheduled recon flight, huh?

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:55.010
What’s wrong?

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:57.720
When Simoun sibyllae take to the sky…

00:06:57.720 --> 00:06:59.020
…she is “praying to the skies.”

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:03.520
Controlling a Simoun is
“speaking with a Simoun.”

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:08.630
Right, we took off to speak with
our Simouns and pray to the skies.

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:10.990
Isn’t that right, Para-sama?

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:15.780
We’re to be back at base at noon.
Till then, don’t forget to be vigilant.

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:21.000
It’s a mouse! A mouse, a mouse!

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:23.450
Where? Where?

00:07:23.450 --> 00:07:24.790
No way.

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:27.700
You mean there are mice on board?

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:33.490
Aren’t you scared, Aer?

00:07:33.490 --> 00:07:37.730
Well, I grew up on a farm,
so there were lots of mice around.

00:07:37.730 --> 00:07:40.520
Hey, the same goes
for you. Right, Mamina?

00:07:47.430 --> 00:07:48.530
Two o’clock.

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:50.030
So far away.

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:53.490
It’s the third time.

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:56.330
They can really get
on your nerves, huh?

00:07:57.540 --> 00:07:59.820
Para-sama, let’s head back now.

00:07:59.820 --> 00:08:02.790
Right, they’re too far away to pursue.

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:05.080
It’d be wiser to return
and make our report.

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:24.410
I can’t stand living in a room like that.

00:08:24.410 --> 00:08:29.010
Why does Dominüra get
her own room? It’s definitely fishy.

00:08:29.010 --> 00:08:33.580
It was thanks to Dominüra’s pleading
that we were able to board this ship.

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:36.200
You really shouldn’t say such things.

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:37.240
But…

00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:39.740
I’m sick of hearing your
whining and complaining.

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:47.070
Hey, Aer…
Is it true that mice bite people?

00:08:47.070 --> 00:08:48.730
If they’re hungry.

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:50.310
So they do bite!

00:08:50.310 --> 00:08:51.560
Grr!

00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:27.670
Welcome back. So?

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:31.680
We spotted far off what we
believed to be enemy planes.

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:34.170
When they noticed us,
they fled immediately.

00:09:34.610 --> 00:09:35.630
I see…

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:38.520
I don’t like it…

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:41.490
They were so far
we lost them in an instant.

00:09:41.490 --> 00:09:43.020
You should report to me.

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:46.270
Oh, the acting captain is here.

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:51.230
I’ve explained my position.
Would you like to hear it again, Kaim?

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:56.280
Chor Tempest’s regina is Neviril.

00:09:56.280 --> 00:10:00.370
Dominüra is the mediator
between our chor and Wauf…

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:02.840
…the patrol ship Messis’s captain.

00:10:02.840 --> 00:10:04.410
A Chor Tempest comrade.

00:10:05.010 --> 00:10:07.620
Paraietta,
make your report to Dominüra.

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:08.670
All right.

00:10:09.310 --> 00:10:11.880
Everybody! Lunch is ready!

00:10:12.410 --> 00:10:15.010
I heard Mamina made it!

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:35.820
You seem sad, Guragief.

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:37.320
Yes…

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:41.220
To tell you the truth,
I’m feeling very sad.

00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:46.570
However, Anubituf, I was sure
that you’d be feeling the same way…

00:10:47.240 --> 00:10:48.580
I suppose I am…

00:10:49.050 --> 00:10:53.260
Chor Tempest,
those glorious Simoun sibyllae.

00:10:53.260 --> 00:10:56.840
But we’re the ones
who took away that glory.

00:10:58.050 --> 00:11:00.930
No matter what it takes, I’ll save them.

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:05.700
And I shall do everything in my
power to summon them back here.

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:07.030
However…

00:11:07.730 --> 00:11:13.060
Is it really in their best interests to be
called back to the Arcus Prima?

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:16.500
Even I can’t answer that…

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:20.400
Thanks for the meal!

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:22.110
Go ahead!

00:11:22.550 --> 00:11:23.780
Looks delicious!

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:24.870
Smells great.

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:26.790
I’m impressed.

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:27.950
Me too.

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:29.120
It’s making me all warm inside!

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:33.480
It’s delicious.

00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:35.130
It tastes great.

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:38.340
There’s still plenty,
so you can have seconds.

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:39.840
Okay!

00:11:40.500 --> 00:11:42.630
Mamina, aren’t you eating too?

00:11:42.630 --> 00:11:44.960
Yes, I will.

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:04.360
U-Um…

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:05.950
What is it?

00:12:06.690 --> 00:12:10.280
What happened the other day… I…

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:15.880
Let’s pretend the whole thing never
happened. Is that clear, Mamina?

00:12:17.070 --> 00:12:18.370
Yes…

00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:20.090
Hey, hey,
what are you talking about?

00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:26.850
Oh, you’re so mean.
You could at least tell us, Mamina.

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:28.560
Neviril!

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:29.600
Don’t ask me.

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:31.310
Can I sit here?

00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:44.700
What?

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:48.340
Listen, Mamina…

00:12:48.340 --> 00:12:51.410
I’d like to talk to you
after lunch if you don’t mind…

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:52.910
All right.

00:12:59.310 --> 00:13:01.920
The new sibylla made this?

00:13:01.920 --> 00:13:03.670
Yeah, it’s pretty good.

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:18.940
Mamina?

00:13:20.530 --> 00:13:25.050
You’re pretty late for someone
who called me here, Roatreamon.

00:13:25.050 --> 00:13:27.200
I’m sorry. I got lost…

00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:30.190
On a puny boat like this?

00:13:30.190 --> 00:13:32.700
Oh, never mind.
What did you want to discuss?

00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:40.670
So what is it?

00:13:43.170 --> 00:13:44.390
If you don’t say anything…

00:13:44.390 --> 00:13:45.670
I…

00:13:47.590 --> 00:13:48.930
I…

00:14:00.370 --> 00:14:02.190
Come now, Mamina.

00:14:06.080 --> 00:14:08.240
It’s not that I didn’t
have any feelings for you.

00:14:10.810 --> 00:14:13.160
How can I patch things up?

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:18.500
Patch things up? That sounds
like we were actually friends before.

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:23.060
Till the end, one of us will always
be above and the other below.

00:14:23.060 --> 00:14:24.250
That’s not true.

00:14:24.700 --> 00:14:28.210
Anyway, just what were
you thinking that day?

00:14:28.210 --> 00:14:30.300
That I wanted to be friends…

00:14:30.300 --> 00:14:31.570
Don’t joke.

00:14:31.570 --> 00:14:34.880
And I feel the same way even now.

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:37.270
This conversation is over.

00:14:39.680 --> 00:14:43.740
I was always envious
of those braids of yours.

00:14:44.650 --> 00:14:46.090
But these are…

00:14:46.090 --> 00:14:49.450
You plait your hair because
your parents told you to.

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:55.040
But those things don’t mean
a thing to a child. To me…

00:14:55.590 --> 00:14:57.910
…they were a rich girl’s hairstyle.

00:15:08.100 --> 00:15:10.330
That’s not true…

00:15:16.110 --> 00:15:21.600
Chor Tempest is the chor all Simoun
sibyllae worship and take pride in…

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:24.100
…the finest chor of all.

00:15:24.100 --> 00:15:26.960
On behalf of all Simoun sibyllae…

00:15:26.960 --> 00:15:30.280
…I beg you to consider
preserving Chor Tempest.

00:15:31.230 --> 00:15:35.640
Do you mean
Chor Tempest as sibyllae?

00:15:35.640 --> 00:15:39.750
Or Chor Tempest as
a squadron of warriors?

00:15:40.650 --> 00:15:45.590
You say you want us to preserve
Chor Tempest, but which one?

00:15:45.590 --> 00:15:47.950
Twelve sibyllae…

00:15:47.950 --> 00:15:51.800
…who become each other’s pairs
and draw Ri Majons across the sky.

00:15:52.390 --> 00:15:55.480
There is only one Chor Tempest.

00:15:57.750 --> 00:16:01.020
You were there that day
as well, weren’t you?

00:16:02.230 --> 00:16:05.770
Yes, I heard everything that
went on during that hearing.

00:16:07.070 --> 00:16:11.640
Thanks to Vura and Onasia, Chor
Tempest was saved from disbanding.

00:16:11.640 --> 00:16:14.990
It was also due to your
brilliant speech, Neviril.

00:16:18.210 --> 00:16:22.850
I am not looking to blame
anyone for this war we’re waging.

00:16:22.850 --> 00:16:27.090
No matter how tragic and painful it
is now, I believe it was meant to be.

00:16:27.690 --> 00:16:31.060
Whether or not that is
Tempus Spatium’s will…

00:16:31.060 --> 00:16:34.570
…it makes no difference to me now.

00:16:34.570 --> 00:16:38.890
I no longer even care whether
it’s God’s will anymore.

00:16:40.960 --> 00:16:44.810
However, I do have
one question for you all.

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:49.770
Despite all this, can I still
call myself a Simoun sibylla?

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:52.990
So you overheard that.

00:16:57.850 --> 00:17:01.660
Neviril, I’d like you to select
the next sibyllae to go on patrol.

00:17:02.190 --> 00:17:06.760
All right, next will be two pairs,
you and Rimone, Alty and Floe.

00:17:06.760 --> 00:17:08.120
Very well.

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:10.420
Dominüra.

00:17:11.880 --> 00:17:16.370
The truth is you’re the one
who saved Chor Tempest.

00:17:16.370 --> 00:17:20.380
You negotiated with the council
to keep us, provided we be sent…

00:17:20.380 --> 00:17:23.150
…to the front lines
on this ship, didn’t you?

00:17:23.150 --> 00:17:24.410
Thank you.

00:17:24.410 --> 00:17:28.390
Chor Tempest is the greatest
chor in Simulacrum Kyuukoku.

00:17:28.390 --> 00:17:30.400
There is no doubt about that.

00:17:31.750 --> 00:17:34.110
Still, how can you do such things?

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:09.560
Wow…

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:11.830
That’s pretty neat.

00:18:11.830 --> 00:18:14.450
It’s a keepsake from my grandpa.

00:18:15.030 --> 00:18:16.360
Paraietta, are you here?

00:18:17.260 --> 00:18:18.820
What’s going on, Neviril?

00:18:19.600 --> 00:18:21.320
Something’s been bothering me.

00:18:21.940 --> 00:18:26.670
I’d like you to tell me the enemy’s
behavior in this morning’s patrol again.

00:18:26.670 --> 00:18:28.870
Fine… But what for?

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:33.450
If I recall, you sighted distant traces
of the enemy several times…

00:18:33.450 --> 00:18:36.050
…and they immediately fled.

00:18:36.050 --> 00:18:38.340
We encountered them
three times to be precise.

00:18:39.090 --> 00:18:40.590
What are you getting at, Neviril?

00:18:41.390 --> 00:18:45.100
I wonder if you four
really saw them first.

00:18:46.460 --> 00:18:51.860
Then they spotted us first and
revealed themselves on purpose?

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:54.860
Most likely. Paraietta, we must hurry.

00:18:55.430 --> 00:18:56.820
I’ll notify the captain.

00:18:57.480 --> 00:19:00.450
The rest of you,
hurry to the flight deck.

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:03.350
Forgive me, Neviril.
It never occurred to me.

00:19:03.350 --> 00:19:06.330
Your scouting flight
path has been tracked.

00:19:06.910 --> 00:19:10.330
Dominüra and the others are being
ambushed. We’re at the border.

00:19:10.930 --> 00:19:14.340
We’re at the front lines
of the enemy’s assault.

00:19:18.320 --> 00:19:20.510
Mamina and
Roatreamon aren’t here yet.

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:21.470
All right.

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:25.470
I’m the auriga.
Kaim, please pair with me.

00:19:25.840 --> 00:19:27.060
Right!

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:30.060
— Yun, you’re my sagitta.
— Right.

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:32.810
Get a move on, Morinas.

00:19:32.810 --> 00:19:34.020
Waporif.

00:19:34.870 --> 00:19:38.280
I’ll send Mamina and Roatreamon
as soon as they arrive.

00:19:49.590 --> 00:19:53.500
What will you do,
Sibylla Roatreamon, Sibylla Mamina?

00:19:53.500 --> 00:19:54.960
The others have already left.

00:19:55.700 --> 00:19:56.960
Mamina, let’s hurry.

00:19:57.530 --> 00:20:01.670
No! I’m not going to pair
with you! Didn’t I tell you before?

00:20:03.730 --> 00:20:05.680
Over my dead body.
It’s never going to happen.

00:20:13.520 --> 00:20:15.360
W-What are you doing?

00:20:19.440 --> 00:20:23.910
W-What… What do you
think you’re doing, Roatre?

00:20:24.620 --> 00:20:26.660
You called me that
when we were little too.

00:20:30.490 --> 00:20:32.040
Sibylla Roatreamon…

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:37.540
Everyone’s in danger…
They could all die…

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:44.680
This is no time for us
to be hesitating, Mamina!

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:03.950
Let’s go, Roatre.

00:21:04.630 --> 00:21:06.410
Yes, Mamina.

00:21:10.600 --> 00:21:12.940
Emergency positions!

00:21:12.940 --> 00:21:14.090
Yes, sir!

00:21:25.580 --> 00:21:29.760
You’re still sniveling?
We’re on our way to meet the others.

00:21:29.760 --> 00:21:31.510
That’s not it… That’s not it.

00:21:31.510 --> 00:21:35.770
It’s just that I’ve always,
always worn braids…

00:21:37.480 --> 00:21:38.520
There they are!

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:51.740
Now’s our chance!
We can take on that many.

00:21:51.740 --> 00:21:52.910
The Iron Ri Majon!

00:22:12.600 --> 00:22:13.640
That meat…

00:22:15.600 --> 00:22:16.640
It was delicious.

00:22:19.600 --> 00:22:20.650
It was the mice.

00:22:41.160 --> 00:22:47.870
<i>It is played by my wounds…
the song of prayer.</i>

00:22:47.870 --> 00:22:52.110
<i>Let it ring out over
the grieving universe.</i>

00:22:52.110 --> 00:22:59.150
<i>Can we change tomorrow?
Don’t be afraid.</i>

00:22:59.150 --> 00:23:06.810
<i>I want to let you know
how my heart’s overflowing.</i>

00:23:15.590 --> 00:23:19.670
<i>“I want to get closer to you.”
“I want to feel your pulse.”</i>

00:23:19.670 --> 00:23:24.840
<i>I was too defiant,
and I took the long way around.</i>

00:23:24.840 --> 00:23:28.850
<i>The blue moon is swaying silently.</i>

00:23:28.850 --> 00:23:32.820
<i>My true heart’s desire is you.</i>

00:23:32.820 --> 00:23:38.720
<i>I can’t reach you.
My tears of pain trickle down.</i>

00:23:38.720 --> 00:23:44.270
<i>Soar away into the sky, song of prayer.</i>

00:23:44.270 --> 00:23:47.700
<i>Carrying my love that came too late.</i>

00:23:47.700 --> 00:23:53.370
<i>What can I do to change tomorrow?</i>

00:23:53.370 --> 00:23:59.890
<i>Just hold on to “now” the way it is…</i>

00:24:04.920 --> 00:24:06.630
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:24:06.630 --> 00:24:11.220
It’s our job as sibyllae
to take the soldiers near that town.

00:24:14.920 --> 00:24:16.790
Next time on Simoun…

00:24:15.470 --> 00:24:19.970
<b>United Front</b>

00:24:16.790 --> 00:24:18.260
United Front.
